---

## What I Learned & Known Issues

* **`add` writes `5` instead of `15`:** When `add x3, x1, x2` runs right after the `addi` instructions, `x3` ends up with `5` instead of `15`[cite: 8] because there is no forwarding or stall logic yet to handle back-to-back data dependencies.
* **`X` values at the end:** Once the `PC` moves past the loaded instructions (around `74.5 ns`), uninitialized memory locations propagate `X` through the pipeline[cite: 7, 8].
* **Next steps:** Leaving this repo as my baseline v1 build and taking what I learned about pipeline timing and hazards into my next, more complete processor project.
